      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. To get them comfortable with renewal, the proposed proof plan was to update index weighting and add a mapping layer translating new taxonomy terms to old query terms, then run an A/B test on the top 20 saved searches. The goal was to achieve a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80% for prioritized queries within 7\u201310 business days, with validation in staging and a conditional credit on renewal if the proof did not meet the agreed uplift. This plan included a 90-day professional services engagement at $48k (with a 30% discount if Orchestrator expansion was signed), and a commitment to compatibility testing with EN-RULES-ENGINE automations and suppression policies [art_8b0063fbb3cb][art_0bccc580184e][art_bd3560dfe194].",
