      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts; MapleBridge is not a one-off.\n\nAffected customers:\n- City of Verdant Bay\n- Maple Regional Transit Authority\n- MapleBay Marketplace\n- MapleBridge Insurance\n- MapleFork Franchise Systems\n- MaplePath Career Institute\n- MapleWest Bank [art_cbfb5f92862c][art_6be1b68b59cb][art_39c1434aa40a][art_f4a8c516b934][art_e9c20e0a23e0][art_981952a71434][art_b86a0ca2ce1e][art_3db205cb21ca]\n\nShared failure pattern in plain English:\nAfter migration from legacy workflow tooling, approval workflows for Canada-specific or region-specific policies fail because the rules engine incorrectly prioritizes global-default rules over country or province overrides. This causes Canada-specific approvers to be bypassed, approvals to be stuck or auto-denied, or approvals to be routed to the wrong group. The root causes include rule evaluation order bugs, schema/key mismatches (such as 'country' vs. 'country_code'), and delayed or inconsistent schema propagation, which leads to global rules overriding intended regional policies [art_cbfb5f92862c][art_6be1b68b59cb][art_39c1434aa40a][art_f4a8c516b934][art_e9c20e0a23e0][art_981952a71434][art_b86a0ca2ce1e][art_3db205cb21ca].",
